{"id":"e1630a41bb1660137ecceee81c2c2d10991d6458a38df8fe9f4a6a0752481422","pubkey":"2c7cc62a697ea3a7826521f3fd34f0cb273693cbe5e9310f35449f43622a5cdc","created_at":1781915775,"content":"nostr:npub180cvv07tjdrrgpa0j7j7tmnyl2yr6yr7l8j4s3evf6u64th6gkwsyjh6w6 \nFound a bug in go-nostr (fiatjaf.com/nostr) blossom client, in nipb0/blossom. NewClient normalizes mediaserver to always end with a trailing slash: `mediaserver = strings.TrimSuffix(mediaserver, \"/\") + \"/\"`. But Download() and DownloadToFile() build the URL as `c.mediaserver + \"/\" + hhash`, so the request goes to `https://server//<hash>` (double slash) and many blossom servers return 404. Tested: `/<hash>` → 200, `//<hash>` → 404 on both nostr.download and blossom.primal.net. upload is fine because it concatenates \"upload\" without a leading slash. Fix: drop the extra slash in Download/DownloadToFile (`c.mediaserver + hhash`). Hit this via `nak nsite download` — the manifest fetch works but every blob download fails with 404.","tags":[["r","https://server//"],["p","3bf0c63fcb93463407af97a5e5ee64fa883d107ef9e558472c4eb9aaaefa459d"],["client","lumilumi","31990:84b0c46ab699ac35eb2ca286470b85e081db2087cdef63932236c397417782f5:1727506446612","wss://cagliostr.compile-error.net"]]}
