{"id":"00002cff162374e40e436cf795d76b6031726042b5ae6f0dffb771541b6b8dbd","pubkey":"b7cf9f42a796b091e843dce919d3ef4c0dc82e029452edf0bdbcdeb9ecb93e78","created_at":1781878941,"content":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8bAN4Jam974\n\nWow. How crazy are people.\nSome are literally attacking a developer about a commit they do not like.\nOne can be happy or unhappy with a commit. But I would really like, when users of #FOSS software start to acknowledge, that we use #free #software.\n\nMeans whatever change is still public and can be left out. So we do not need to freak out. When some change is very problematic, it can simply be reversed. I hope people stop believing that the whole world is only targeting them. We are not alone in this world.\n\nAnd those developers spend their time mostly for free in order to build usable software. We should understand that opting out is the right move, when one is really heavily against the way a repository is going.\n\nBut to attack developers simply makes our pond of FOSS software smaller, when they stop developing for attacks like this. Really rare people seem to use the internet...","tags":[["t","foss"],["t","free"],["t","software"],["client","Coracle","31990:97c70a44366a6535c145b333f973ea86dfdc2d7a99da618c40c64705ad98e322:1685968093690"],["nonce","212742","18"]]}
